KF.Y TO THE SPECIES OF MYCENELLA IN WESTERN EUROPE
1,0 $ Spores without warts (but occasionally with one or two germ tubes). $ M. salicina
1,2 $ Spores with conspicuous warts.

2,3 $ Spores < 10 um. with rounded warts.
2,0 $ Spores > 10 µm with large conical warts.
2,0,N$/// ===> Voir : Xerula kuehneri

3,0 $ Apex of cystidia with simple or branched projections. $ M. margaritispora
3,4 $ Apex of cystidia without projections.

4,5 $ Cheilo- and pleurocystidia lageniform with a long cylindrical neck with non-mucronate. obtuse apex. Basidia 2-spored.
4,6 $ Cheilo- and pleurocystidia fusiform with subacute or mucronate apex. Basidia mostly 4 spored.

5,0 $ Stipe grey-brown. $ M. bryophila var. bryophila
5,0 $ Stipe blueish grey. $ M. bryophila var. caesia

6,0 $ Lamellae and upper part of stipe with small reddish spots. Cheilo- and pleurocysdidia frequently mucronate. $ M. rubropunclala
6,0 $ Without small red spots. Pleuro- and Cheilocystidia not mucronate. $ M. trachyspora

